1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:08,230
One HTTP request. One hundred and one SELECTs.

2
00:00:08,230 --> 00:00:13,000
Counted by instrumentation, not guessed.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:19,190
1 list query: all 100 articles.

4
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:26,420
Then 100 author lookups, one per article.

5
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:30,940
100 articles, 12 authors.

6
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:39,980
One author fetched 14 times; 88 lookups repeat.

7
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:46,450
Fix: one explicit JOIN, ORDER BY article id.

8
00:00:46,450 --> 00:00:49,690
Same fields. No loop.

9
00:00:49,690 --> 00:00:54,960
Same 100 articles, same order, same shape.

10
00:00:54,960 --> 00:01:00,230
The two JSON bodies are byte-for-byte equal.

11
00:01:00,230 --> 00:01:05,910
Flawed: 101 SELECTs. Corrected: 1.

12
00:01:05,910 --> 00:01:15,010
Control: a hidden extra query shows as 102.

13
00:01:15,010 --> 00:01:21,530
We counted queries. We did not measure speed.

14
00:01:21,530 --> 00:01:29,680
The interface made one request. The backend multiplied the work.
